; xinput1_4_diag.def -- the diagnostic build's export source (build.ps1 -Diag): every line
; of xinput1_4.def after its first, plus sh_diag_status at ordinal 300 and the script notes
; (sh_diag_note 301, sh_diag_note_listening 302) for the development daemon (diag_status.h).
; tests/diag_status_test.c checks that the two agree.
;
; The backend ships as XINPUT1_4.dll. DOOM 2016 (April 2024 update, Steam build 13954591)
; imports exactly two functions from it BY ORDINAL: 2 (XInputGetState) and 3 (XInputSetState).
; MSVC's __declspec(dllexport) numbers exports ALPHABETICALLY, which once put
; XInputGetBatteryInformation at 2 and corrupted the heap on every controller poll; the bodies in
; xinput_proxy.c therefore carry no dllexport.
;
; This is the real System32 XINPUT1_4.dll ordinal set (Windows 11 26200): the named exports at
; their ordinals and the unnamed ones (100-104, 108, 109) as NONAME forwarders, so anything that
; resolves an XInput 1.4 ordinal from the game folder reaches the system implementation.
; Ordinal 1 is the system DLL's DllMain and is not exported. The proxy exports nothing else.
EXPORTS
    XInputGetState                  @2
    XInputSetState                  @3
    XInputGetCapabilities           @4
    XInputEnable                    @5
    XInputGetBatteryInformation     @7
    XInputGetKeystroke              @8
    XInputGetAudioDeviceIds         @10
    sh_xinput_ordinal_100           @100 NONAME
    sh_xinput_ordinal_101           @101 NONAME
    sh_xinput_ordinal_102           @102 NONAME
    sh_xinput_ordinal_103           @103 NONAME
    sh_xinput_ordinal_104           @104 NONAME
    sh_xinput_ordinal_108           @108 NONAME
    sh_xinput_ordinal_109           @109 NONAME
    sh_diag_status                  @300
    sh_diag_note                    @301
    sh_diag_note_listening          @302 DATA
    sh_diag_hold_entity             @303 DATA
